## Finding

**Medium | docs/agents/team/TEAM.md:231 | evidence | concrete correction**

Evidence: the Codex follow-up example is
```sh
codex exec -m gpt-5.6-sol -s read-only resume <id> --json - \
  < <follow-up-prompt> > collab/<task>-r<n>.gpt-5.6-sol.stdout.log
```
`codex exec resume --help` lists no `-s`/`--sandbox` option, and passing `-s read-only` *after* `resume` errors (`error: unexpected argument '-s' found`). Placed *before* `resume` (as written) it's silently accepted by the parent `exec` parser, but nothing in the CLI's own help confirms that flag is actually applied to the resumed session — `resume` documents no sandbox concept at all. The doc's Security section requires the read-only guarantee to actually hold on follow-ups, so implying it's preserved here isn't backed by CLI evidence. (This ordering already existed in the pre-image's abstract table entry `codex exec [-s <mode>] resume <id> -`; this diff is the first place it's promoted into a concrete, copy-pasteable command.)

Correction: drop `-s read-only` from the follow-up example, and state the actual guarantee in prose, e.g. "Codex resume reuses the sandbox policy recorded with the original session; it cannot be overridden on resume" — or, if that can't be confirmed, add an explicit caveat instead of a command implying control the CLI doesn't expose.

